1
00:00:03,190 --> 00:00:05,910
Leonard, I've been working on an opening joke

2
00:00:05,910 --> 00:00:07,490
for our lecture at Berkeley.

3
00:00:07,760 --> 00:00:08,850
Oh, I like to laugh.

4
00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:10,780
But say it anyway.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:13,380
Okay, um...

6
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:15,970
What do you say to a graduate

7
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:18,310
of the UC Berkeley physics department?

8
00:00:18,310 --> 00:00:20,650
I'll have fries with that.

9
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,570
Because his education hasn't prepared him

10
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:25,850
for a career in the sciences.

11
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:28,890
You know, when they chase you out of there,

12
00:00:28,890 --> 00:00:31,300
you only have to run faster than Sheldon.

13
00:00:31,810 --> 00:00:33,120
Are you all set for your trip?

14
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,330
Yeah, I think so.

15
00:00:34,330 --> 00:00:37,530
I just restocked the old PRK.

16
00:00:37,530 --> 00:00:38,480
"P.R.K"?

17
00:00:38,480 --> 00:00:40,800
Public restroom kit.

18
00:00:41,920 --> 00:00:43,830
Everything a boy needs for making pee pee

19
00:00:43,830 --> 00:00:46,320
in new and strange places.

20
00:00:46,730 --> 00:00:49,030
I don't see what's crazy about bringing a backpack

21
00:00:49,030 --> 00:00:51,060
with your own toilet paper and Purell.

22
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:52,690
Keep going.

23
00:00:52,690 --> 00:00:56,180
And rubber gloves, uh, air freshener.

24
00:00:56,180 --> 00:00:58,360
Um, noise-cancelling headphones.

25
00:00:58,360 --> 00:01:00,230
Oh, danger whistle.

26
00:01:01,170 --> 00:01:02,820
pepper spray.

27
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:06,000
Ooh, a multi-language "Occupied" sign.

28
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:06,930
Uh, let's see.

29
00:01:06,930 --> 00:01:10,380
We have seat protectors, uh, booties for my shoes,

30
00:01:10,380 --> 00:01:12,670
a clothespin for my nose.

31
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:15,660
Oh, and a mirror on a stick,

32
00:01:15,660 --> 00:01:18,060
so I can make sure the person in the stall next to me

33
00:01:18,060 --> 00:01:20,420
isn't some kind of weirdo.

34
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:24,580
You still worried some Berkeley girl

35
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:26,260
is gonna steal him away?

36
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:29,440
Yes, who do you think gave him the danger whistle?

37
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,620
Would you like to play a physics car game I invented

38
00:02:00,620 --> 00:02:02,860
called "I Can't Spy"?

39
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:06,030
It's all the nail-biting tension of "I Spy"

40
00:02:06,030 --> 00:02:08,370
but the added fun of subatomic particles

41
00:02:08,370 --> 00:02:11,280
and waves outside the visible spectrum.

42
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:12,620
If it's half as much fun as

43
00:02:12,620 --> 00:02:14,780
"One Times Ten to the Fourth Bottles of Beer on the Wall,"

44
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:16,420
I'm in.

45
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:18,360
I'll begin.

46
00:02:18,620 --> 00:02:23,280
Uh, I can't spy with my little eye...

47
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:26,490
something passing right through us.

48
00:02:26,490 --> 00:02:28,560
That soy Frappuccino I had.

49
00:02:29,690 --> 00:02:31,220
Will you please play the game?

50
00:02:31,220 --> 00:02:33,700
I can't spy with my little eye

51
00:02:33,700 --> 00:02:35,750
something passing right through us.

52
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:37,910
I don't know, um...

53
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:40,280
If 65 billion solar neutrinos pass

54
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:42,770
through a square centimeter every second,

55
00:02:42,770 --> 00:02:44,670
given the surface area of this car is

56
00:02:44,670 --> 00:02:46,600
about 60,000 square centimeters,

57
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:51,660
that means 3.9 times ten to the 15th solar neutrinos?

58
00:02:53,330 --> 00:02:55,470
I don't want to play anymore.

59
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,620
We haven't been on a road trip in a while.

60
00:02:58,620 --> 00:02:59,470
This is fun.

61
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,690
We get it-- you won the game.

62
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:02,190
Stop bragging.

63
00:03:02,980 --> 00:03:04,900
No, listen, we wrote a paper together.

64
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:06,730
Now we get to go to a university and talk about it?

65
00:03:06,730 --> 00:03:08,790
That's pretty cool.

66
00:03:09,140 --> 00:03:10,970
I suppose it is.

67
00:03:10,970 --> 00:03:15,430
In fact, if you'd like to celebrate with a little music,

68
00:03:15,430 --> 00:03:17,290
I'd be okay with that.

69
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:19,980
What...?

70
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,770
This road trip just got crazy.

71
00:03:24,410 --> 00:03:27,120
Play that funky music, white boy.

72
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:31,010
I'm surprised you know that reference.

73
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:33,750
What reference?

74
00:03:36,940 --> 00:03:39,270
So, I put stickers on everything we're gonna sell.

75
00:03:39,270 --> 00:03:41,520
We just need help taking it all out to the driveway.

76
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,050
Can I be in charge of pricing?

77
00:03:43,050 --> 00:03:45,350
I've been going to garage sales my whole life.

78
00:03:45,350 --> 00:03:48,140
Can you believe I got these pantyhose for a nickel?

79
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,240
All right, Amy's in charge of pricing

80
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:53,390
and being 75.

81
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:56,080
Hey, Penny, can you give me a hand with this?

82
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:56,840
Sure.

83
00:03:56,840 --> 00:03:58,450
Aw, we had one of these growing up.

84
00:03:58,450 --> 00:04:00,010
I used to play all the time.

85
00:04:00,010 --> 00:04:02,220
Oh, yeah? I love Ping-Pong.

86
00:04:02,220 --> 00:04:04,550
Oh, I meant beer pong.

87
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:06,070
I had a table, too,

88
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:07,620
but I didn't have any friends,

89
00:04:07,620 --> 00:04:09,980
so all I did was serve.

90
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:13,320
You know, you can leave one side up and play against it.

91
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:16,060
And if I had a friend, they might have told me that.

92
00:04:19,570 --> 00:04:20,820
Excuse me.

93
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:22,450
Why is there a sticker on this?

94
00:04:22,450 --> 00:04:24,710
It's my TARDIS from Doctor Who.

95
00:04:24,710 --> 00:04:26,860
I was planning on moving it in the house.

96
00:04:26,860 --> 00:04:29,150
I think you just answered your own question.

97
00:04:30,040 --> 00:04:32,510
Come on, one day, this may double in value

98
00:04:32,510 --> 00:04:35,270
and be worth half what I paid for it.

99
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:36,840
Sweetie, we have a lot to do.

100
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:39,010
We don't need to decide this right now.

101
00:04:39,010 --> 00:04:41,760
Well, I guess as long as you're keeping an open mind.

102
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,840
Of course.

103
00:04:48,670 --> 00:04:52,600
* Play that funky music, white boy *

104
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:57,050
* Play that funky music right *

105
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:59,610
* Play that funky music, white boy *

106
00:04:59,610 --> 00:05:01,520
So... they're requesting

107
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:04,920
that the white boy play the funky music, yes?

108
00:05:05,550 --> 00:05:06,880
Yes.

109
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:10,100
And this music we're listening to right now

110
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,960
is funky as well?

111
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,880
Sure.

112
00:05:15,410 --> 00:05:16,860
Let me ask you this.

113
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:18,170
Do you think

114
00:05:18,170 --> 00:05:23,010
this song is the music the white boy ultimately play?

115
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:26,370
It could be.

116
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:30,170
So it's like the musical equivalent of Russell's Paradox,

117
00:05:30,170 --> 00:05:32,840
the question of whether the set of all sets

118
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:36,000
that don't contain themselves as members contains itself?

119
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,960
- Exactly. - Well...

120
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:39,280
then I hate it.

121
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:41,020
Music should just be fun.

122
00:05:43,670 --> 00:05:45,060
Making great time.

123
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,670
Gonna be there pretty early.

124
00:05:47,190 --> 00:05:48,850
Will our hotel room be ready?

125
00:05:48,850 --> 00:05:50,370
I doubt it.

126
00:05:50,970 --> 00:05:52,800
Aren't you worried that sitting in the lobby

127
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,330
for a long period of time

128
00:05:54,330 --> 00:05:58,040
might attract the attention of the hotel detective?

129
00:05:58,830 --> 00:05:59,700
If we do,

130
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:02,810
we'll just tell him to "hit the bricks, see?"

131
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:07,740
Seems a little confrontational, but all right.

132
00:06:09,120 --> 00:06:13,030
You know, we won't be very far from Skywalker Ranch.

133
00:06:13,030 --> 00:06:15,110
Oh, that's true.

134
00:06:15,110 --> 00:06:17,020
It's not like we can get in there.

135
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:18,450
Why not?

136
00:06:19,030 --> 00:06:20,810
I-I don't think George Lucas put his headquarters

137
00:06:20,810 --> 00:06:21,840
in the middle of nowhere

138
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:24,440
because he wanted people dropping in.

139
00:06:24,890 --> 00:06:28,090
Yoda's swamp was in the middle of nowhere.

140
00:06:28,090 --> 00:06:30,540
Tatooine was in the middle of nowhere.

141
00:06:30,540 --> 00:06:33,540
Hoth was in the middle of nowhere.

142
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:35,430
That's code, Leonard.

143
00:06:35,430 --> 00:06:37,570
He wants us to drop in.

144
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,410
We do have time.

145
00:06:41,410 --> 00:06:44,430
I mean, we could drive by and just look at it.

146
00:06:44,430 --> 00:06:45,930
Yes! Oh...

147
00:06:46,380 --> 00:06:48,250
I'm so excited.

148
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:50,490
And I just can't hide it.

149
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:55,470
"I'm about to lose control, and I think I like it."

150
00:06:56,650 --> 00:06:59,300
What are you talking about?

151
00:07:04,490 --> 00:07:06,650
So when do you guys think you're gonna move in?

152
00:07:06,900 --> 00:07:09,460
We're still figuring how much remodeling we want to do.

153
00:07:09,460 --> 00:07:11,340
It's tricky finding the right balance between

154
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:15,360
"Tasteful modern" and "Jewish mother tchotchke crapfest."

155
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:18,700
Have you made a decision about the TARDIS?

156
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,130
I think I can sell it if we call it,

157
00:07:20,130 --> 00:07:22,660
"Big British Porta-Potty."

158
00:07:24,760 --> 00:07:27,050
We're not selling it-- it's mine.

159
00:07:27,050 --> 00:07:28,540
You can't just decide.

160
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:30,250
How about I arm-wrestle you?

161
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:31,400
That's not fair.

162
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:36,060
It's like me challenging you to a sexy pants contest.

163
00:07:36,970 --> 00:07:38,650
You could play Ping-Pong for it.

164
00:07:38,650 --> 00:07:39,860
I would do that.

165
00:07:39,860 --> 00:07:40,710
How is that fair?

166
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:41,910
You grew up with a table.

167
00:07:41,910 --> 00:07:44,430
Yes, but I mostly used it as a battlefield

168
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:47,340
in an ongoing war between the Transformers and the ThunderCats

169
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,530
for control of a bra I had found in the woods.

170
00:07:51,530 --> 00:07:53,570
Bernadette, for every episode of Doctor Who

171
00:07:53,570 --> 00:07:54,950
Leonard has made me sit through,

172
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:56,270
I will play on your behalf

173
00:07:56,270 --> 00:07:58,340
and send that TARDIS back to Gallifrey,

174
00:07:58,340 --> 00:08:00,850
where I hate that I know it belongs.

175
00:08:01,330 --> 00:08:03,330
Yes, Penny plays for me.

176
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:06,630
That's not fair-- she has upper body muscles.

177
00:08:07,430 --> 00:08:10,400
Dude, three-time Sanskriti School

178
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:13,820
for Well-Born Boys badminton champion.

179
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:16,320
That's right-- okay, Raj can play for me.

180
00:08:16,320 --> 00:08:17,810
Ooh, you just chose champions.

181
00:08:17,810 --> 00:08:19,940
It's like we're reenacting the ancient German practice

182
00:08:19,940 --> 00:08:21,800
- of trial by combat. - Yeah, it's also like

183
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:24,310
when the Mountain fought the Red Viper in Game of Thrones.

184
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,950
Leonard makes you watch that, too?

185
00:08:25,950 --> 00:08:27,000
No, no, I like that show.

186
00:08:27,000 --> 00:08:29,480
It's got dragons and people doing it.

187
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:31,640
So it's settled.

188
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:34,090
The fate of Doctor Who's TARDIS will be decided

189
00:08:34,090 --> 00:08:36,590
by a Game of Thrones inspired death-match on the battlefield

190
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:39,880
of ThunderCats versus Transformers.

191
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:43,090
If you still have that bra, I'll give you a nickel for it.

192
00:08:49,610 --> 00:08:52,030
There it is.

193
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:55,010
It's just a gate.

194
00:08:55,460 --> 00:08:57,710
On a road.

195
00:08:58,300 --> 00:09:00,850
Wasn't even that hard to find.

196
00:09:03,310 --> 00:09:04,530
This is so amazing!

197
00:09:04,530 --> 00:09:05,880
I know!

198
00:09:07,830 --> 00:09:09,010
You want to get a picture?

199
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:10,470
I want more than a picture.

200
00:09:10,470 --> 00:09:11,690
I want to go in.

201
00:09:11,690 --> 00:09:13,940
Well, so do I, but they'll never let us.

202
00:09:14,330 --> 00:09:17,080
Is that the attitude that helped you get Penny?

203
00:09:17,080 --> 00:09:18,770
No, but I don't have three years

204
00:09:18,770 --> 00:09:21,510
to make that gate feel sorry for me.

205
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:25,130
Uh, there's a speaker box.

206
00:09:25,130 --> 00:09:26,690
Drive up, push the button,

207
00:09:26,690 --> 00:09:28,650
and let's see what happens.

208
00:09:30,080 --> 00:09:31,330
Okay, yeah.

209
00:09:31,330 --> 00:09:33,090
What do we have to lose?

210
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:43,330
I'm a little nervous.

211
00:09:43,330 --> 00:09:45,580
Well, get over it.

212
00:09:45,580 --> 00:09:48,480
Confidence is key in these situations.

213
00:09:48,480 --> 00:09:49,400
Right.

214
00:09:51,380 --> 00:09:54,040
You pushed it-- are you out of your mind?!

215
00:09:56,190 --> 00:09:57,080
May I help you?

216
00:09:57,080 --> 00:09:59,600
Uh, uh... we don't have an appointment,

217
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:00,540
and-and we don't belong here,

218
00:10:00,540 --> 00:10:03,400
but we-we're, like, crazy-big fans.

219
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,070
I mean...

220
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:07,080
"Crazy for Star Wars" crazy,

221
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:09,940
not crazy like we have a backpack full of duct tape,

222
00:10:09,940 --> 00:10:11,440
although we do have a backpack

223
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:13,920
that you really don't want to look in.

224
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,490
You're blowing it.

225
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:19,300
We want to meet George Lucas

226
00:10:19,300 --> 00:10:22,510
and become his friends and play with him!

227
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:25,490
Hello?

228
00:10:25,490 --> 00:10:27,800
This speaker's not working, just pull up.

229
00:10:32,270 --> 00:10:34,560
And that's how it's done.

230
00:10:43,160 --> 00:10:47,440
All right, we've defeated the first challenge.

231
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:50,900
Now we must steel ourselves to face the monster

232
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,780
who defends the gate.

233
00:10:54,110 --> 00:10:56,110
We're trying to get past a security guard,

234
00:10:56,110 --> 00:10:58,300
not rescue Zelda.

235
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:02,060
I think what really needs to be rescued is your sense of whimsy,

236
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:04,080
but one quest at a time.

237
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:07,050
So what's the plan?

238
00:11:07,050 --> 00:11:10,020
Uh, I'm just gonna be honest with the guy.

239
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:12,310
Honesty will never get us in.

240
00:11:12,310 --> 00:11:13,980
Well, what's your plan?

241
00:11:13,980 --> 00:11:17,170
All right, my plan is predicated on the assumption

242
00:11:17,170 --> 00:11:19,140
that they have a nurse's office

243
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:22,860
and your willingness to be lightly stabbed.

244
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:31,520
Who are you here to see?

245
00:11:31,520 --> 00:11:33,290
Uh, I'm just gonna tell you the truth.

246
00:11:33,290 --> 00:11:35,290
Oh, you are killing me.

247
00:11:35,860 --> 00:11:37,570
We don't have an appointment.

248
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:39,710
We-we're just fans of Mr. Lucas's work,

249
00:11:39,710 --> 00:11:40,950
and we thought we'd take a shot

250
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:43,140
and see if we could get in and look around.

251
00:11:43,140 --> 00:11:44,590
Sorry, guys, we get this a lot.

252
00:11:44,590 --> 00:11:45,700
Can't let you in.

253
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:49,600
What if I told you that I was the voice of Yoda?

254
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:54,620
A recording session I must attend.

255
00:11:56,200 --> 00:11:57,550
I'm sorry, don't listen to him.

256
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,070
We're actually physicists.

257
00:11:59,070 --> 00:12:00,880
We're giving a lecture at Berkeley later today.

258
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:03,210
We just... we had some time to kill.

259
00:12:03,210 --> 00:12:05,100
Hey, listen, you seem like decent guys.

260
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:06,430
I can't let you in,

261
00:12:06,430 --> 00:12:08,630
but I got some hats and T-shirts I can give you.

262
00:12:08,630 --> 00:12:10,530
Thank you so much.

263
00:12:11,130 --> 00:12:12,420
See?

264
00:12:12,420 --> 00:12:13,870
Maybe honesty is the best...

265
00:12:13,870 --> 00:12:15,180
What are you doing?

266
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:16,610
Shedding the yoke of my oppressors,

267
00:12:16,610 --> 00:12:19,150
you blind, sad little man.

268
00:12:19,150 --> 00:12:20,560
Don't move!

269
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:23,090
Code A-A-23, A-A-23.

270
00:12:23,090 --> 00:12:24,370
Copy.

271
00:12:24,370 --> 00:12:26,400
I can see the ranch, Leonard!

272
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,900
Oh, it's rustic, it's lovely.

273
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:32,930
I'd take a picture, but people are chasing me.

274
00:12:33,350 --> 00:12:34,600
I'm gonna make it...!

275
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,900
I'm gonna make it!

276
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:38,550
They have Tasers, but they wouldn't dare use...

277
00:12:43,050 --> 00:12:44,740
Come on, Raj.

278
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:48,560
You are the King Kong of Ping-Pong.

279
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:51,910
You are the menace of table tennis.

280
00:12:52,300 --> 00:12:55,230
Put her away, 'cause I don't have a third one.

281
00:12:56,290 --> 00:12:57,460
Yes!

282
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:00,260
Rajesh eight, Penny four.

283
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:02,030
Sorry, he's really good.

284
00:13:03,010 --> 00:13:04,410
Hey, Raj.

285
00:13:04,410 --> 00:13:05,900
if Howard can't keep the TARDIS,

286
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:07,630
how great would it look at your place?

287
00:13:07,630 --> 00:13:08,290
What?

288
00:13:08,290 --> 00:13:10,470
Yeah, what?

289
00:13:11,010 --> 00:13:12,730
I don't know much about Doctor Who,

290
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:16,270
but if, um, you were to put this right outside your front door

291
00:13:17,370 --> 00:13:18,840
and open up the back,

292
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:21,070
it would be like your entire apartment was

293
00:13:21,070 --> 00:13:23,430
the inside of the TARDIS,

294
00:13:23,430 --> 00:13:24,700
which is pretty cool

295
00:13:24,700 --> 00:13:27,510
'cause on the show, the inside of the TARDIS

296
00:13:27,510 --> 00:13:29,610
is bigger than the outside.

297
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:34,350
But then again, I don't know much about Doctor Who.

298
00:13:35,950 --> 00:13:37,140
Don't listen to her.

299
00:13:37,140 --> 00:13:40,120
You and I go way back-- we're like brothers.

300
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:42,880
We are. We are.

301
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,070
Oh, no! What a terrible serve!

302
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:50,610
Sorry, brother.

303
00:13:50,610 --> 00:13:51,940
- Eight-five. - This is ridiculous.

304
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:53,060
I want a new champion.

305
00:13:53,060 --> 00:13:55,690
Amy, were you serious about being able to serve?

306
00:13:55,690 --> 00:13:58,530
Uh, it-it's been a long time.

307
00:13:58,530 --> 00:14:00,100
I don't know.

308
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:02,300
I'm probably pretty rusty.

309
00:14:06,740 --> 00:14:07,890
She's my champion!

310
00:14:07,890 --> 00:14:10,060
Well, if you can switch champions, so can I.

311
00:14:10,060 --> 00:14:11,550
- I want Raj. - Hey.

312
00:14:11,550 --> 00:14:13,060
Oh, come on, like you even care.

313
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,480
I care!

314
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:16,330
Oh, wait, no, I don't. Good luck, Raj.

315
00:14:18,750 --> 00:14:21,560
You know, I thought our friendship meant more to you.

316
00:14:22,150 --> 00:14:23,780
So did I.

317
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:32,960
Do you think they're gonna call the police?

318
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:34,270
I don't know.

319
00:14:35,600 --> 00:14:37,520
Maybe they'll call Imperial Officers to take us

320
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:40,420
to a holding cell on the Death Star.

321
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:46,290
Oh, I think that's below the pay grade of an Imperial Officer.

322
00:14:46,290 --> 00:14:47,380
Stormtroopers are really the ones who...

323
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:49,510
Oh, shut up.

324
00:14:50,350 --> 00:14:51,780
He's right.

325
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:53,920
Uh, Stormtroopers actually combine both the function

326
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:56,710
of infantry and military police.

327
00:14:58,410 --> 00:15:00,290
Uh-huh, I'm normally very nice,

328
00:15:00,290 --> 00:15:02,760
but you shut up, too.

329
00:15:08,630 --> 00:15:10,750
So...

330
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,850
what are you in for?

331
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:17,220
Honestly, I just wanted to meet Mr. Lucas and say thank you.

332
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:20,600
You know, growing up, the movies had such an impact on my life.

333
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,570
I never really fit in anywhere.

334
00:15:22,570 --> 00:15:24,890
Till I discovered the worlds he created

335
00:15:24,890 --> 00:15:27,370
and finally found a place where I belong.

336
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,290
But why are you here?

337
00:15:31,050 --> 00:15:32,510
Oh, I, uh, I hopped a fence,

338
00:15:32,510 --> 00:15:33,700
and they caught me in the sculpture gallery

339
00:15:33,700 --> 00:15:36,710
making out with a Chewbacca statue.

340
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:44,420
Excuse me.

341
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:54,510
Leonard,

342
00:15:54,840 --> 00:15:57,310
they have a sculpture gallery.

343
00:16:01,440 --> 00:16:02,860
All right, I talked to my supervisor,

344
00:16:02,860 --> 00:16:04,840
and we're gonna let you go with a warning.

345
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,030
But if you ever come back,

346
00:16:06,030 --> 00:16:07,800
we will call the police and press charges.

347
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:08,770
We understand.

348
00:16:08,770 --> 00:16:10,050
Thank you so much.

349
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:11,260
Uh, what about me?

350
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:13,240
No, you're not going anywhere, kissy face.

351
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:14,680
Let's go.

352
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,230
I have to take your picture to post at the guard gate.

353
00:16:17,700 --> 00:16:19,530
Uh, one question about that picture.

354
00:16:19,530 --> 00:16:21,970
Can it be with George Lucas?

355
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:25,880
Ooh, grumpy you are.

356
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:33,470
Okay, this is the match that decides it all.

357
00:16:33,470 --> 00:16:34,680
First to 11 wins.

358
00:16:34,680 --> 00:16:37,780
Serve switches every five points.

359
00:16:37,780 --> 00:16:39,530
And just so you know, when this started,

360
00:16:39,530 --> 00:16:42,090
I was going to put the TARDIS in a discreet corner of the house,

361
00:16:42,090 --> 00:16:43,330
but I've since turned mean,

362
00:16:43,330 --> 00:16:45,150
and now it's going right in the middle of the living room

363
00:16:45,150 --> 00:16:47,250
on a rotating platform with a sign that says "Suck it".

364
00:16:47,250 --> 00:16:48,670
Game on.

365
00:16:50,840 --> 00:16:52,000
Except...

366
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,830
Raj is gonna win.

367
00:16:53,830 --> 00:16:55,290
Isn't that right, Raj?

368
00:16:55,610 --> 00:16:57,700
Uh, yeah, I mean, her serve was pretty good.

369
00:16:57,700 --> 00:16:59,260
Come on, get in her head.

370
00:16:59,260 --> 00:16:59,980
Be intimidating.

371
00:16:59,980 --> 00:17:02,020
Okay, uh...

372
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:03,940
I'm gonna own you, bitch!

373
00:17:05,450 --> 00:17:06,960
That's not nice.

374
00:17:08,030 --> 00:17:09,650
Let's just play.

375
00:17:13,450 --> 00:17:14,910
One-zero.

376
00:17:15,330 --> 00:17:16,430
Two.

377
00:17:16,860 --> 00:17:18,050
Three.

378
00:17:18,580 --> 00:17:19,810
Four.

379
00:17:20,380 --> 00:17:22,240
Five-nothing.

380
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:24,320
Wait, did you play badminton

381
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:26,520
or sad-minton?

382
00:17:27,580 --> 00:17:29,790
Don't listen to him-- all she's got is a serve.

383
00:17:29,790 --> 00:17:32,920
Now, grab a fresh tampon and put her away.

384
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:33,670
Wha...?

385
00:17:33,670 --> 00:17:35,280
A-And that's not offensive?

386
00:17:35,280 --> 00:17:36,310
Where's the line?

387
00:17:36,310 --> 00:17:38,400
It's in your purse. Play.

388
00:17:41,480 --> 00:17:42,480
One-five.

389
00:17:43,400 --> 00:17:44,460
Two-five.

390
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:46,480
Three-five.

391
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,240
Four-five.

392
00:17:49,070 --> 00:17:50,680
Five-five!

393
00:17:52,050 --> 00:17:53,030
Six.

394
00:17:53,470 --> 00:17:54,610
Seven.

395
00:17:54,610 --> 00:17:55,960
Eight.

396
00:17:56,410 --> 00:17:57,710
Nine.

397
00:17:58,500 --> 00:18:00,360
Ten-five!

398
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:03,670
Six.

399
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:05,860
Seven.

400
00:18:07,210 --> 00:18:08,110
Eight.

401
00:18:08,760 --> 00:18:09,720
Nine.

402
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:12,230
Ten-ten!

403
00:18:16,330 --> 00:18:18,850
Well, that was an exciting 40 seconds.

404
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:22,790
It was, and now the serve is back to you,

405
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,710
and the game is over.

406
00:18:25,370 --> 00:18:27,730
You know, Amy, I, uh...

407
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:30,370
can't help but wonder how Sheldon would react

408
00:18:30,370 --> 00:18:33,390
if the TARDIS was at your place.

409
00:18:33,390 --> 00:18:35,900
Don't listen to her, just hit the ball.

410
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:37,530
Keep talking.

411
00:18:42,270 --> 00:18:44,510
If this doesn't get him into your bedroom,

412
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:46,610
nothing will.

413
00:18:52,690 --> 00:18:53,830
Are you still mad at me?

414
00:18:53,830 --> 00:18:58,130
Yes, we missed our lecture, we were almost arrested,

415
00:18:58,130 --> 00:18:59,790
and you got me locked in a room with a man

416
00:18:59,790 --> 00:19:03,070
who forced his tongue down the throat of a stuffed Wookie.

417
00:19:05,020 --> 00:19:07,940
Boy, some people are just glass-half-empty.

418
00:19:08,390 --> 00:19:09,940
The glass is empty, Sheldon.

419
00:19:09,940 --> 00:19:11,080
It's completely empty.

420
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:13,150
If you gave that glass to a man who was dying of thirst,

421
00:19:13,150 --> 00:19:15,110
he would be dead, do you know why?

422
00:19:15,110 --> 00:19:18,720
Before I answer, was he a smoker?

423
00:19:22,980 --> 00:19:25,230
I think you're looking at this all wrong.

424
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:27,760
Fine, then tell me how I should be looking at it.

425
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:32,270
Well, not only did we go to Skywalker Ranch, we got in.

426
00:19:32,270 --> 00:19:34,560
And no one we know can say that.

427
00:19:34,560 --> 00:19:37,740
And for all the times you find me irritating,

428
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:41,490
today you got to watch someone shoot me with a Taser.

429
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,640
That part was pretty good.

430
00:19:47,160 --> 00:19:48,480
See?

431
00:19:49,030 --> 00:19:51,610
You did flop around a lot.

432
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,830
I'll take your word for it.

433
00:19:53,830 --> 00:19:56,590
I was too busy trying not to defecate.

434
00:19:58,820 --> 00:20:02,410
You know, when they were escorting us to the detaining room,

435
00:20:02,410 --> 00:20:04,060
I looked through a door,

436
00:20:04,060 --> 00:20:06,280
and I'm pretty sure I saw a display case

437
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:08,360
with the Ark of the Covenant.

438
00:20:08,360 --> 00:20:10,530
- That's amazing. - I know.

439
00:20:10,530 --> 00:20:14,590
And I saw Jabba the Hutt riding by on a motorcycle.

440
00:20:14,590 --> 00:20:16,490
Although that was right after the Tasing,

441
00:20:16,490 --> 00:20:18,470
so who can say for sure?

442
00:20:19,710 --> 00:20:22,380
I-I guess this could count as an adventure.

443
00:20:22,380 --> 00:20:23,840
It was.

444
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:26,590
And even though we're not allowed back there,

445
00:20:26,590 --> 00:20:29,350
they can never take today away from us.

446
00:20:29,350 --> 00:20:31,540
Unlike my sense of smell,

447
00:20:31,540 --> 00:20:34,190
which hasn't returned since the Tasing.

448
00:20:36,830 --> 00:20:38,230
No, I got nothing.

449
00:20:44,860 --> 00:20:47,850
Amy, the Daleks are right on my tail!

450
00:20:47,850 --> 00:20:49,990
Quick, we need to reset the time circuits.

451
00:20:50,320 --> 00:20:53,740
Oh, no, I left my sonic screwdriver behind.

452
00:20:58,030 --> 00:20:59,880
Really should have thought this through.

